  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2017) position from Southeast Bank's own audited annual report multi-year \"Key Financial Data and Ratios\" summary table. CONSOLIDATED (Group) basis. Southeast Bank prepares its multi-year \"Key Financial Data and Ratios\" summary tables on the consolidated basis, so no Solo/Standalone multi-year series exists in these reports; this was verified against the underlying statements (FY2025 total assets 554,424.56m consolidated vs 551,643.08m solo, a 0.50% difference; FY2014 236,608.40m consolidated vs 236,216.15m solo, 0.17%). The bank's subsidiaries (Southeast Bank Capital Services, SBL Exchange entities) are small relative to the bank, so the consolidated series tracks the solo series closely, but the basis differs from the Solo-basis series used for banks elsewhere in this dataset. Total liabilities are calculated as total assets minus total shareholders' equity (the source tables do not print a total-liabilities line). Net interest income is calculated as Interest Income minus Interest Expenses. Provision for Loans is calculated as Provision for Unclassified Loans plus Provision for Classified Loans. Total Expenditure is Interest Expenses plus Operating (Non-Interest) Expenses throughout. The composition of Total Income changes with the table format: for FY2011-FY2019 Investment Income is a separate line that sits alongside Non-Interest Income, so Total Income = Interest Income + Investment Income + Non-Interest Income (verified: FY2014 19,233.89 + 5,274.27 + 3,158.93 = 27,667.09 = reported Total Income; FY2019 26,258.88 + 5,288.98 + 4,844.75 = 36,392.61 = reported Total Income). From FY2020 the tables fold Investment Income into Non-Interest Income, so Total Income = Interest Income + Non-Interest Income (verified: FY2023 22,047.89 + 14,118.37 = 36,166.26 = reported Total Income). Investment Income is still reported separately in both formats and is retained as its own line item here, so for FY2020 onwards it must not be added to Non-Interest Income when reconstructing Total Income. Reserve fund is calculated as Total Shareholders' Equity minus Paid up Capital (25,823.65 - 9,169.50); the source table's \"Reserve Fund & Surplus\" row (24,595.63) reproduces Total Capital (33,765.13), not equity. EPS is recorded as 1.27, the figure reported contemporaneously in the FY2017 report and the one consistent with its own inputs (net profit 1,168.63 over the 916.95m shares outstanding at end-2017, and 22.20 / 1.27 = the 17.42 Price Earnings Ratio the same table reports); the FY2018, FY2019 and FY2021 reports all restate FY2017 EPS as 1.11, the same profit spread over FY2018's larger 1,054.49m share count. The FY2022 report separately restates the FY2017 P/E as 6.66, which is a duplicate of its own FY2018 value.",
